## Final-pass security guarantees proven live (`07_security_tests.log`)

- **Item 1** — `TCREATE1/2/3` (direct INSERT rejected on all three tables),
  `TDEL1/2/3` (direct DELETE rejected), `TPROT1–4` (protected identity/commercial
  columns not client-updatable), `TSAFE` / `TSAFE_LINE` (safe operational columns
  still work). **Targeted integrity patch:** `TQTY_DENIED` + `TQTY_UNCHANGED`
  (client cannot UPDATE line quantity; failed attempt leaves the row unchanged),
  `TSOFTDEL_PET` + `TSOFTDEL_LINE` (client cannot set deleted_at on a pet or a
  line, and the failed attempt does not modify the row), `TQTY_EFFECTS`
  (commission base = unit_price × authoritative quantity = 100×3 = 300; inventory
  consumption = recipe qty × authoritative quantity = 2×3 = 6 — effects use the
  unchanged authoritative quantity).
- **Item 2** — `TBRANCH_READ_*` (branch-restricted user sees only its branch;
  `branches.all` sees both), `TBRANCH_UPD` (cross-branch update hits zero rows),
  `TBRANCH_RESERVE` (cross-branch reserve denied `wrong_branch`),
  `TBRANCH_RESERVE_OK` (own-branch reserve succeeds).
- **Item 3** — `TREL_CANCEL` / `TREL_NOSHOW` (reservation released, availability
  restored, no silent consumption), `TREL_IDEMP` (terminal-state re-transition
  rejected → no double-release).
- **Item 4** — `TCACHE_INS` / `TCACHE_UPD` (booking cache columns not client-
  writable on INSERT or UPDATE).

