## Local-PostgreSQL limitations / Supabase verification still required

- This is a **local PostgreSQL 16.14** run, not the target managed/Supabase
  environment. RLS behaviour under the real `authenticator` → `authenticated`
  JWT switch (via PostgREST) should be confirmed there; here it is simulated
  with `set local role authenticated` + `request.jwt.claims`.
- The `authenticated` role here is a bare nologin role; a managed platform may
  attach additional default grants or a different search_path. Re-run this same
  clean-room against a staging Supabase project before promoting.
- Base tables such as `subscriptions` may carry extra NOT-NULL columns in your
  environment; the fixtures seed the minimum this engine requires.
- No `0014`, SDK, backend, or UI work is included or implied. The governed
  support-access path (platform-admin visibility, privileged repair) is
  explicitly deferred to `0014` and is intentionally absent here.
